{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:20:31.258593Z","id":"2f7a336048d42e9054c59a718a0ca00aab3b53c6ab481c2b7c94cce8bb81a477","body":{"detail":"The tokens use color-mix() (Chrome 111+) for --k-accent-soft, --k-hero-from/to and the badge, button and FAB tints, and the bars use backdrop-filter. A WebView older than Chrome 111 drops every declaration that uses color-mix, so the tonal buttons, selected tab pill and hero gradient lose their color. Verified so far: Playwright Chromium at 390x844, light and dark, against a scratch daemon (target/kit-shots/v3/*.png at the time). Next: load apps/clax_app/assets/kit/example/index.html in the app on a device and compare.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"8165007a82858fce58d8f90516ef6c8ff9ad6489e75a476be212ee0103cb0be9"},"summary":"kit.css is verified in desktop Chromium only, not in an Android WebView","tags":["unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:20:31.258777Z","id":"5f2c634a6962c4df52cc8232439dd97fb7961884d51c83d97d5da7fc8044b935","body":{"detail":"TabBar falls back to the tab whose path is '/' when no tab's path is a prefix of the route, so a pushed screen outside every tab shows Home selected. Apps that nest pushed screens under a tab path (/activity/item/3) are marked right.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"e9f8d1f4c4a18723740c0a5c9df72c0983e4b466e8c59e18d9b470b502619960"},"summary":"On a screen that is not a tab (such as /settings) the tab bar marks the '/' tab as current","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.470851Z","id":"e5d4920d17ec8780c9a61e4bd07c3c65670e3eb17eae6561bd3f913d4e0bd0ad","body":{"detail":"Failure: any Button variant=\"gradient\" in dark mode. .k-btn.k-gradient sets color:#fff while the dark accents are light (#7c9bff default, about 2.6:1; the example's #3ddbb0/#2bb6c9, under 2:1). target/kit-shots/v3/settings-dark.png shows the Save label washing out. The FAB and filled button use --k-on-accent and read fine.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":294},"end":{"line":294},"content_hash":"8e51c0c68efd3ab111a61759f199ac35f63206c93897d0b53a927fb9839a6b04"},"suggested_fix":"color: var(--k-on-accent) (and the same for any other hard-coded #fff over the accent).","summary":"Gradient buttons hard-code white text, illegible on a bright dark-mode accent","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.470959Z","id":"4515ed2c0bd3423aa995d3b9a27fb0ceeb9f6d4cb7570320fb0677f3fce85a75","body":{"detail":"Failure: any tabbed screen with a Fab and a List that reaches the bottom. .k-main pads var(--k-tab-h)+var(--k-s6) = 88px; the FAB (kit.css:478-489) spans from 72px to 128px above the bottom, so at full scroll the last row's amount and chevron sit under it (target/kit-shots/v3/home-light.png shows the overlap mid-list). Content also shows through the 0.82-alpha tab bar (insights-light.png: bars visible under the tab labels), which reads as a glitch.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"3628b6590ecf0b42dfe829205f1c09861740004ffb2794a161c2d358aa34a385"},"suggested_fix":"Pad .k-main by a further 56px+gutter when a FAB is present (.k-app:has(.k-fab) .k-main, or a class App sets), and raise --k-bar alpha (about 0.94) so content under the tab bar is a tint, not legible text.","summary":"Bottom padding does not clear the FAB, so the last row's trailing value stays under it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471008Z","id":"7668a9052db4792bab6c91ec54f2fba025e2b7ab8150bd3620033ea453556ec2","body":{"detail":"Failure: AppBar large on any screen (home, activity, insights in the example). In large mode the bar row keeps --k-bar's distinct background and full --k-bar-h height while its title is hidden (kit.css:240), so the top shows a tinted strip holding only the actions, or nothing (target/kit-shots/v3/insights-light.png, home-light.png). Wasted space at the most valuable part of a phone screen; looks unfinished.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"04798c73f26cb2528c8331f83a259609faea5f58eb20c584d305710cebf33933"},"suggested_fix":"While .k-large-mode is not scrolled, make the bar transparent (no background or backdrop) and, when there is no lead and no actions, collapse the row (or put actions on the large title's line) so the large title starts near the top.","summary":"A large-title AppBar leaves an empty 52px band above the title","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471052Z","id":"1ba1e0457381cd00c7e8c164991eeeca6106fc07dfd78e053474fa2979150965","body":{"detail":"--k-fg-3 (#9696a0 light on --k-bar #f9f9fb, about 2.9:1; #6f6f78 dark on #161618, about 3.6:1) at 10.5px is below WCAG 4.5:1 for small text; inactive tabs look disabled in target/kit-shots/v3/*.png.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":257},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"4d8e805db6a935787bc21a8b66599a170236f3fe2a6d227ba1af1ef4505d68c4"},"suggested_fix":"Use --k-fg-2 for inactive tab labels, keep fg-3 for icons only if wanted.","summary":"Inactive tab labels are 10.5px at about 3:1 contrast","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471109Z","id":"ac1e69d30de5adcd135ed172d4553f8ee0ab74fb424a644eeeec0abff48139f3","body":{"detail":"save/add/set/update/remove return the db promise; a rejection (invalid_argument for a non-object save(null) or an update on a missing doc, quota_exceeded, revoked; web/contract/0.2.61/db.d.ts:115-160) becomes an unhandled rejection and the UI shows nothing; the hooks' error state only reflects subscription errors. Memory mode diverges too: update on a missing doc silently no-ops (kit.js:643) where db rejects, and merges shallowly where db merges nested objects.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":655},"content_hash":"507a3a1e34a2a8e4cb77774290f3f631bfe96fb81ab4d7f83c470d8cefaf0d14"},"suggested_fix":"Catch in the hooks: set state.error and toast(e.message, {tone:'danger'}) by default, still rejecting for callers that await.","summary":"Write failures from useDoc/useCollection are silent unless every caller catches","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471161Z","id":"3ee3da0d1c0b7a51d532769b0eceecc4a4426873027a2e29ad641e6e34f7a6e2","body":{"detail":"getDb() resolves null whenever use('db') does (docs/contract.md: undeclared capability, outside the viewer). Nothing tells the model or the render step that data is not persisting.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":513},"end":{"line":522},"content_hash":"710b5eaa6ea75de9e2421b700340fb7640c3b1edee0fe78a2514c804d9e7f049"},"suggested_fix":"console.warn once when falling back while window.claude exists (the render tool's console capture then surfaces it).","summary":"The memory fallback is silent, so an app that forgot to declare db looks fine and loses every write on reload","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471200Z","id":"3774506165981d2ba689f534810a215a40dfafae6ac9a88423be993a7860b24a","body":{"detail":"A model that imports back and writes back=${back} passes a function: backTo === true is false, so go(fn) throws on path.startsWith. Also useDoc returns a tuple while useCollection returns an object, an easy mismatch to guess wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"4ece0bbdfd811ede0891f455cdeaa7c2c87bd5cfe4db88340df618cd51307357"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a function for back (call it), and document both return shapes prominently in the add_kit result.","summary":"AppBar's back prop shares its name with the exported back() function","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471232Z","id":"c354e26c673d8facc5fd740255a1917f63f202f7a035e43f1aeea8192dcf97d1","body":{"detail":"preact.js and dates.js were built with --legal-comments=none and icons.js carries a one-line attribution only. MIT (preact, dayjs) and ISC (Lucide) require the copyright and permission notice in copies; Apache-2.0 (htm) requires the licence text. add_kit copies these files into every published app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"5148fd7d4e6d9014c41cf0e631737f27afb9757155ae91ac3cce762d756982cf"},"suggested_fix":"Prepend a short header to each vendored file (package, version, SPDX ID, copyright line) and add kit/LICENSES.txt with the full texts, copied by add_kit with the kit part.","summary":"Vendored third-party code ships without its licence notices","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.623319Z","id":"982691988c91c8dccf844e133131554756da5c68bc006598e9fdc78aca769dee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"preact.js, dates.js and icons.js open with a header naming package, version, licence and copyright; assets/kit/LICENSES.txt holds the MIT, Apache-2.0 and ISC texts and kitParts copies it with each vendored part (test/agent/tools/kit_tool_test.dart passes).","supersedes":"c354e26c673d8facc5fd740255a1917f63f202f7a035e43f1aeea8192dcf97d1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.624442Z","id":"63c5e15c9edd2fdd593fb8235d9c4139cada1e9d4ebc55c93fa2cb5b044114d3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"kit.css pads .k-main:has(.k-fab) by the FAB's height plus the gutter (and the tab bar when tabbed); --k-bar is 0.94 alpha. target/kit-shots/v4/home-bottom-dark.png: the last row (Rent, $1,200.00) clears the FAB at full scroll.","supersedes":"4515ed2c0bd3423aa995d3b9a27fb0ceeb9f6d4cb7570320fb0677f3fce85a75","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.625372Z","id":"1f1195d3018ab96c8f40116d9484aa9981c98d7a2fd6fda3f0381e8ae5c52cfb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"In large mode the AppBar is fixed and transparent until scroll, and .k-large-title.k-bare drops the bar height when the bar has no buttons (kit.js AppBar bare). target/kit-shots/v4/insights-dark.png (no band) and home-bottom-dark.png (compact bar after scroll).","supersedes":"7668a9052db4792bab6c91ec54f2fba025e2b7ab8150bd3620033ea453556ec2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.626278Z","id":"280e66f359c11a5d610612b9fab1791808a4239568822fac513b5a9f884f71a6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Inactive tab labels are 11px in --k-fg-2 (#5c5c66 on #f9f9fb, about 6.5:1; #a9a9b3 dark, about 8:1); see target/kit-shots/v4/*.png.","supersedes":"1ba1e0457381cd00c7e8c164991eeeca6106fc07dfd78e053474fa2979150965","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.627172Z","id":"555437850eca5651c583c0ca9a37ae8e03dd921f39103b719e5b50c5a8906fa1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"kit.css .k-btn.k-gradient now uses color: var(--k-on-accent); target/kit-shots/v4/settings-dark.png shows the Save label dark on the bright gradient.","supersedes":"e5d4920d17ec8780c9a61e4bd07c3c65670e3eb17eae6561bd3f913d4e0bd0ad","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.628078Z","id":"8259d2710ac96dcaca44a04400b6f26ddc3aeab007d639c43abb5d143dcee3b2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"TabBar no longer falls back to the '/' tab; target/kit-shots/v4/settings-dark.png shows no tab current on /settings.","supersedes":"5f2c634a6962c4df52cc8232439dd97fb7961884d51c83d97d5da7fc8044b935","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.628960Z","id":"60518f902883136523f9e59ec777f84c3351a70dc56b665a978d3a055ca50f24","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppBar back now takes true, a path or a function (back=${back} works); useDoc returns {data, save, ready, error} like useCollection's object, and the add_kit API text says so.","supersedes":"3774506165981d2ba689f534810a215a40dfafae6ac9a88423be993a7860b24a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.629833Z","id":"ca26c79f7310a2dac7499650b725c35b1548ba4f612605bf0fb078be4cea235e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"getDb() logs one console.warn naming the missing {\"db\": {}} declaration when use('db') resolves null (kit.js getDb).","supersedes":"3ee3da0d1c0b7a51d532769b0eceecc4a4426873027a2e29ad641e6e34f7a6e2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.630708Z","id":"f5764276098669b812b738e011e67093aefe21c704ead87af8c26fc56b0a68f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"serial() in kit.js shows a danger toast and rethrows on any write failure, so the caller's promise rejects; memory update rejects on a missing document and merges nested objects (deepMerge), as db does.","supersedes":"ac1e69d30de5adcd135ed172d4553f8ee0ab74fb424a644eeeec0abff48139f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:03:50.989328Z","id":"37c67e6ee4063e2689234914e3c36bb6bc255a53a7fe2fa1047c7a0fabf8f967","body":{"detail":"net.fetch takes no abort signal (web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts ClaxExtensions.Net), so pump() only skips tiles no map wants any more before they start; up to CONCURRENCY (6) fetches for tiles panned away still run to the end, and their tiles are cached. A fast fling at high zoom therefore delays the tiles now in view by up to one round of stale fetches. An abort through the shell (a request ID the bridge can cancel) would remove the wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"d2fdd54eadd0f414bfa6e0ddb135b059577e5b8b217ed8d61eaa28168d9ea55b"},"summary":"A tile fetch already started cannot be cancelled","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:03:50.989369Z","id":"9f0b8dce5736de95cabd7a64beefc286cd38da4da9f96a97270d7ff1be05d267","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/map.spec.ts drives drag, keyboard zoom, a marker click and the consent flow in Chromium; WebKit was only screenshotted. Two-finger pinch (pointer events with setPointerCapture on the container), double-tap and touch-action: none inside the app's WebViews are unverified on a device.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":393},"content_hash":"ae8f77ebf1ad2547433b931cf417e74e58aac0023fbb0e9a348b5801a7e69962"},"summary":"The map's gestures are tested in Chromium and drawn in Playwright WebKit, not yet in the Clax app's WKWebView or Android WebView","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:03:50.989402Z","id":"c2697bc489f0d6c86da7ba092b5814bd23ff744755997c7064feac23e2945682","body":{"detail":"The map fetches tiles at round(zoom) and scales them by 2^(zoom - round(zoom)); OpenStreetMap serves only 256 px tiles. Fetching one zoom level deeper when devicePixelRatio >= 2 (four times the tiles, so four times the requests to the tile host) would sharpen them; it was left out to keep the load on tile.openstreetmap.org low.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":398},"content_hash":"9c87d06bc4fc1a7e06f622b2269705d811504fccb02bca96f136e357fb4bb757"},"summary":"Tiles are drawn at one CSS pixel per tile pixel, soft on 2x and 3x screens and between whole zoom levels","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:58.384519Z","id":"9b274f05b3fe70688d7ccc932e94eca5f6f9833f2d56b389e7bc5694329b60b8","body":{"detail":"The LRU here (CACHE_MAX 300 blob: URLs) lives for one page load, and the daemon's fetch (crates/clax-server/src/net.rs) has no HTTP cache, so Cache-Control/Expires on tiles are ignored and reopening a map, or every view of it, fetches the same tiles again. The OSM tile usage policy (operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles) asks for caching that honours the tile server's headers (it suggests at least 7 days). At prototype scale the load is small; with many users all sharing one User-Agent (USER_AGENT, net.rs line 37) a block would take maps away from every Clax user at once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"569c16ec924e676872af7c9f52ecf5168f3bbb64ae8be41c6b1140561b92197f"},"suggested_fix":"A small disk cache in the daemon for GET responses with cacheable headers (keyed by URL, bounded in size, honouring max-age/Expires and revalidating with ETag/If-Modified-Since), or at least a per-app tile cache in the shell keyed by URL.","summary":"Tiles are cached only in the page's memory: every app open re-downloads every tile from tile.openstreetmap.org, which OpenStreetMap's tile usage policy asks clients to avoid","tags":["review","osm-policy","K3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:58.384567Z","id":"a6c9c2a7c6a973567fa12f8699eda39abce247de414aebd8e72fb351e2e8cf19","body":{"detail":"load() caches a failure with its time and pump() skips it for RETRY_MS (15 s), but pump() runs only on a view change (the urlKey effect, line 420) or when another fetch ends (line 128). After an upstream_error, timeout or HTTP 5xx/429 on every visible tile, nothing is in flight and nothing schedules a pump, so the 'Map tiles did not load; retrying.' note (line 486) stays until the person moves the map.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"a8bdefec5ef0f1af65e92850a3905be6333c4cbb1f8c029cf90ccd8517b99e5b"},"suggested_fix":"When load() records a non-terminal failure, setTimeout(pump, RETRY_MS) (one timer at a time).","summary":"A failed tile is retried only when something else calls pump(), yet the map says 'retrying'","tags":["review","K3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:58.384606Z","id":"09c429d63828d057b617df5a20a1a4a8e955cd00bcada835116340ffe6d71ef7","body":{"detail":"pinSvg(color) interpolates m.color into fill=\"...\" and line 471 sets it as innerHTML, so a color taken from data (a db document another viewer wrote, a net answer) such as '\"/><image href=x onerror=...>' runs script in the page, with its capabilities. Colors usually come from the app's own code, but the API invites data-driven colors.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"058891e41089374fe1b4ee4f4bf82a38ace107ede2c59404a511f4161699276e"},"suggested_fix":"Strip [\"<>&] from color (as icons.js line 120 does for label), or set the fill through a style/CSS variable on the button instead of markup.","summary":"A marker's color goes unescaped into SVG markup set with dangerouslySetInnerHTML","tags":["review","security","K3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.703474Z","id":"5a1a6d418926a435d4653bba91563d6dd933ed43df278b53884e3c497e06d1d6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: the pin's fill is var(--k-map-pin), set as a style property through the DOM, and m.icon reaches icon() only when it names a known icon. web/e2e/map.spec.ts \"a marker's color and icon from data never become markup\" passes (no <img>, window.pwned unset, a valid color fills the pin) and fails on the previous map.js.","supersedes":"09c429d63828d057b617df5a20a1a4a8e955cd00bcada835116340ffe6d71ef7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.705124Z","id":"69b16136fb9ef1be2ffd55ad1b89670c1b511b8a059ac0c73820f9a4623c7c05","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: a failed tile backs off 1 s doubling to 15 s, and pump() arms a timer for the earliest backoff end. web/e2e/map.spec.ts \"tiles that fail are tried again on a timer, without the map moving\" passes, and fails on the previous map.js.","supersedes":"a6c9c2a7c6a973567fa12f8699eda39abce247de414aebd8e72fb351e2e8cf19","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.706598Z","id":"4bd231f9787bfa62d4453b5234afd39705b4a8a369ed25bc4b73c48f805b954a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: crates/clax-server/src/net_cache.rs, a 100 MiB LRU disk cache under CLAX_HOME/net-cache honouring max-age/s-maxage/Expires and revalidating with ETag/Last-Modified. cargo test -p clax-server --lib net: 16 passed (hit, 304 revalidation, no-store/private/Set-Cookie/Vary:* bypass, credentialed bypass, size cap).","supersedes":"9b274f05b3fe70688d7ccc932e94eca5f6f9833f2d56b389e7bc5694329b60b8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:03:33.855472Z","id":"02a847e0d4a4a3f6484bc6aa07e933fca9a3f1b3cc7f74f02b6835e9f6b1f1c8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: every color-mix() in kit.css now sits in @supports (color: color-mix(in srgb, red, red)) after a plain fallback, so a WebView before Chrome 111 keeps every tint, hero and shadow; //design:tokens_sync fails on a color-mix() outside @supports (scripts/test-sync-tokens.sh case 9). bazelisk test //scripts:sync_tokens //design:tokens_sync //web:unit PASSED; bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='kit|home app|map|over a fake host|renders' PASSED (28 passed). The fallback path was rendered in headless Chromium with the @supports condition made false: tonal buttons, badges, hero, toast and FAB keep their colours in light and dark.","supersedes":"2f7a336048d42e9054c59a718a0ca00aab3b53c6ab481c2b7c94cce8bb81a477","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.982211Z","id":"1541218705136734af72e89cd7b0a952338791336566574bec7ec77fd3c578aa","body":{"detail":"In dark --k-danger is #ff8a80 and --k-accent #7cc36f. .k-tab-badge (kit.css:327-330), .k-btn.k-danger (:348) and .k-item-lead (:413-416) set color: #fff on them. --k-on-accent exists (#141413 in dark) but is unused here, and there is no --k-on-danger (design/tokens.json onError is #141413 in dark). The dark danger became lighter in this phase (it was #ff6b6b).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":327},"end":{"line":330},"content_hash":"263a7008b6d7dabb2a56135c48d8413efd0060add82384beea496893bb740d89"},"suggested_fix":"Map --k-on-danger to onError and use --k-on-accent / --k-on-danger in these rules.","summary":"Kit rules hard-code #fff text on --k-danger and --k-accent, which are light in dark mode: 2.28:1 and 2.12:1","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:52.422431Z","id":"36329810c21ab0c5cda4f1974eec3f2a10b06408f524c290ef2bf758d6cce1ea","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"--k-on-danger maps to on-danger (#141413 in dark, pair on-danger on danger in design/tokens.json); the tab badge and danger button use it and the item lead --k-on-accent. kit.spec.ts's contrast test failed before in dark (danger 2.28) and passes: `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=kit.spec` exit 0.","supersedes":"1541218705136734af72e89cd7b0a952338791336566574bec7ec77fd3c578aa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:43.536874Z","id":"2f118309414cf42337f20cd3a62af3f4b4465dc02771c302d1374129aa319675","body":{"detail":"In the home app this left a drag's scroll clamped and a new group's name field unfocused; apps/clax_app/home/home.css works around it with transition-property: none on .h-page, .h-name and .h-name-input (commit f1c07f346b12). Any other kit page or app that changes a property and reads its result in the same task under reduced motion meets the same delay.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"357cd698170dc0eb2fcce4afd61cf6e964a32cd2bb66f845672b2f25df16187f"},"suggested_fix":"Limit the rule to elements that declare a transition, or set transition-property: none alongside the duration where an element's transitions are not wanted","summary":"With reduced motion every element transitions every property over 1 ms (transition-property defaults to all), so a change a page reads or uses in the same render (layout for a scroll, visibility for a focus) arrives a moment late","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:58.295661Z","id":"0effaa9caa6e1709c9c25e143c43cb1caf1fe968d6f206e9a3cb12a3f69c0116","body":{"detail":"The map fetches tiles at round(zoom) and scales them by 2^(zoom - round(zoom)); OpenStreetMap serves only 256 px tiles. Fetching one zoom level deeper when devicePixelRatio >= 2 (four times the tiles, so four times the requests to the tile host) would sharpen them; it was left out to keep the load on tile.openstreetmap.org low.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":522},"end":{"line":525},"content_hash":"9c87d06bc4fc1a7e06f622b2269705d811504fccb02bca96f136e357fb4bb757"},"summary":"Tiles are drawn at one CSS pixel per tile pixel, soft on 2x and 3x screens and between whole zoom levels","supersedes":"c2697bc489f0d6c86da7ba092b5814bd23ff744755997c7064feac23e2945682","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:42.002307Z","id":"a3af6d01906de13e21f3070b9a218e4e8d79a91786ea97c46ea104ab913cd3a5","body":{"detail":"net.fetch takes no abort signal (web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts ClaxExtensions.Net), so pump() only skips tiles no map wants any more before they start; up to CONCURRENCY (6) fetches for tiles panned away still run to the end, and their tiles are cached. A fast fling at high zoom therefore delays the tiles now in view by up to one round of stale fetches. An abort through the shell (a request ID the bridge can cancel) would remove the wait.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":181},"content_hash":"c9b1ac8391cfbb9f3e3a526dc72592caa7816ceb5f6552ef0ee09ee9e1be97d6"},"summary":"A tile fetch already started cannot be cancelled","supersedes":"37c67e6ee4063e2689234914e3c36bb6bc255a53a7fe2fa1047c7a0fabf8f967","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:42.107414Z","id":"e6c0c057c0b5501d5660777a8ec3a4c0d4f3ddc04b38ba765cf5764b58698b12","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/map.spec.ts drives drag, keyboard zoom, a marker click and the consent flow in Chromium; WebKit was only screenshotted. Two-finger pinch (pointer events with setPointerCapture on the container), double-tap and touch-action: none inside the app's WebViews are unverified on a device.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"168b3bccbd587a43fab8e8ba174e7fd7b4c76932ceb5d217e47772002a0dcd61"},"summary":"The map's gestures are tested in Chromium and drawn in Playwright WebKit, not yet in the Clax app's WKWebView or Android WebView","supersedes":"9f0b8dce5736de95cabd7a64beefc286cd38da4da9f96a97270d7ff1be05d267","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
